## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to add a real, cross-DC capability using Docker Configs, a TLS edge (Traefik), and a simple stateful component (Redis). It also touches observability (metrics) and inter-DC consistency via pub/sub.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant rate limiting with Redis counters
- Docker Configs for per-tenant quotas
- Cross-DC synchronization via Redis Pub/Sub
- TLS termination with Traefik edge proxy
- Metrics exposure for Prometheus

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rate-limit middleware sketch
const quota = getQuotaFromConfig(req.headers['X-Tenant']);
const key = `rl:${tenant}:${windowStart}`;
let count = redis.incr(key);
if (count === 1) redis.expire(key, windowSeconds);
if (count > quota) {
  res.status(429).set('Retry-After', String(windowSeconds)).send('Too Many Requests');
} else {
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test burst traffic and quota drift across DCs?
- What strategies ensure accurate time windows across replicas?
- How would you monitor per-tenant usage and alert on anomalies?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement data governance and privacy in a multi-DC setup: edge TLS, per-tenant policy, hot-reload, and observability with Loki, all integrated via docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- Traefik edge TLS termination across DCs
- Middleware-based response redaction per-tenant
- Docker Config hot-reload and policy delivery
- Loki-based centralized logs with per-tenant retention
- X-Tenant routing and impact on latency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Express-style middleware skeleton for redacting response payloads per-tenant policy
function redactor(policy) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const oldSend = res.send;
    res.send = function (body) {
      let payload = typeof body === 'string' ? JSON.parse(body) : body;
      const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
      const p = policy[tenant] || { redact: [] };
      if (payload && typeof payload === 'object') {
        for (const key of p.redact) {
          if (payload.hasOwnProperty(key)) payload[key] = 'REDACTED';
        }
      }
      oldSend.call(this, JSON.stringify(payload));
    };
    next();
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test hot-reload correctness and no-downtime guarantees for policy updates?
- How would you measure and mitigate the performance impact of redaction on large payloads?
